tests/game/six-car-race.test.ts:31-40 and tests/game/six-car-grid.test.ts:48-57 both contain:
```
const world = createWorld(getTrack(trackId), { seed, carCount: 6 });
const bots = world.cars.map((_, i) => createBot(world, i));
const inputs: CarInput[] = [];
for (let i = 0; i < LIMIT && world.racers[0]?.finishTick == null; i++) {
  const tickInputs = bots.map((b) => b.input(world));
  inputs.push(tickInputs[0] as CarInput);
  stepWorld(world, tickInputs);
}
```
The only differences are the tick limit (`FIVE_MINUTES` vs `60 * 60 * 10`) and an extra `expect` in the grid file. Line 2 is exactly the body of `botsFor(world)` in tests/sim/helpers.ts:62-64 (`return world.cars.map((_, i) => createBot(world, i));`). The clone detector missed the copy because each run is under 6 lines.
